Now take the running coupling \eqref{eq:running_alpha}. Laplace-transform \eqref{eq:evolution_general} in $Y$ and show that
$\widetilde\Phi(t,\omega)$ satisfies the inhomogeneous ODE
\begin{equation}\label{eq:laplace_ode_inhom}
\omega\,\widetilde\Phi(t,\omega)-\Phi_0(t)=\frac{1}{b\,t}\left(\chi_0\,\widetilde\Phi(t,\omega)+\frac{\chi_2}{2}\,\partial_t^2\widetilde\Phi(t,\omega)\right).
\end{equation}
Then write down the corresponding homogeneous equation (drop $\Phi_0$).

Consider the homogeneous ODE \eqref{eq:airy_form_pre} on $t\in[0,\infty)$.
Impose the boundary conditions
\begin{equation}\label{eq:dirichlet_bc}
\widetilde\Phi(t,\omega)\text{ decays as }t\to\infty,\qquad \widetilde\Phi(0,\omega)=0.
\end{equation}
(i) Show that the change of variables
\begin{equation}\label{eq:s_change}
s=\left(\frac{\omega}{A}\right)^{1/3}\left(t-\frac{B}{\omega}\right)
\end{equation}
reduces \eqref{eq:airy_form_pre} to the Airy equation $\phi''(s)-s\phi(s)=0$.
(ii) Conclude that the decaying solution is proportional to $\mathrm{Ai}(s)$.
(iii) Derive the discrete eigenvalue condition and solve for $\omega_n$ in terms of Airy zeros $a_n$.

Take the running coupling \eqref{eq:running_alpha}. Laplace-transform \eqref{eq:evolution_general} in $Y$, then write down the corresponding homogeneous equation (drop $\Phi_0$).
Assume a Robin/matching condition at $t=0$:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:robin_bc}
\widetilde\Phi(t,\omega)\text{ decays as }t\to\infty,\qquad
\widetilde\Phi'(0,\omega)+r\,\widetilde\Phi(0,\omega)=0,
\end{equation}
where $r$ is a fixed real constant.
Do a change of variable
\begin{equation}\label{eq:s_change}
s=\left(\frac{\omega}{A}\right)^{1/3}\left(t-\frac{B}{\omega}\right)
\end{equation}
with $A=\frac{\chi_2}{2b}, B=\frac{\chi_0}{b}$, and derive the Robin quantization condition as an implicit equation for $\omega$ in terms of Airy function.
